@@ f34r
# ======================================================================
<f34r>            <!$I=H $Q=E $P=C $L=B $H=2>
# [ONE-LEG GALLOWS CHECKED]

# Unit <f34r.P1>: Text.
#
# In this file, the alignment between the right and left halves of the
# second paragraph is based on line count, even though the lines on
# the right are shifted down by a varying amount (from 0.5 to 1.5
# times the mean baseline spacing). The misalignment is indicated
# by "{\}" comments.
# Petersen, as well as most transcribers, used an alignment based on
# line position, where the right half of lines 4 through 9 were
# shifted down one line, with the spill over being transcribed as line
# 10. That interpretation seems more contrived than the one adopted
# here; and is only an imperfect solution, since the baselines remain
# substantially misaligned.
# A case could be made for the two halves being independent paragraphs.
# However, that layout would have no parallel among the herbal pages.

<f34r.1;U>         wcheoepchy.olar,yl-<!®>yzody.okedody.shod.ololdy.dar.ytey<|>
<f34r.2;U>          <:>ytar.sheody.olam-<!®>octhedy.otedy.chdain.oltey.kchy,ty<|>
<f34r.3;U>          <:>qotedy.chyty.chdaly-<!®>dar.chd.otedy.qotol.okedy.dody.ody.kam<|>
<f34r.4;U>          <:>ytedy.daiin.chey.aiin-<!®>sho.chckhy-<!®><!\>oltchedy.otedy.dam.checthy<|>
<f34r.5;U>          <:>qoteedy.shedy.shedy.ol-<!®>okes.ar-<!®><!\>ykeedl,chedy.otey.okaiin<|>
